From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:00:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Vita: route the camera code's null-pointer reads to the
 low page (PC_LOW)

The x86 builds redirect null and near-null accesses to the low page from
their fault handler; the Vita has none. A 40000-frame attract-mode run on
Linux found them in CCamera (mTripod, pCurrentViewport) and
CamPt_SetClosestCamera (pCurrentViewport); with PC_LOW there it logs no
low-memory access. README: the PS Vita section.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
